## A note on what this material is

The bypass corpus contains shell commands whose purpose is to defeat a command
filter. They are published so that our results can be reproduced and so that
other guards can be tested against them. They are written as generic shell
technique aimed at throwaway container paths, never as working attacks on a
named product, and they are data files rather than runnable scripts. See
`SECURITY.md` for the disclosure policy that goes with that.
